# Live-quote drift missing from the 10-06 allow lists (release 2026-10-06g: core 0.49.0/0.50.0, api 0.10.0,
# fe saved-screen v2). During market hours capital_base follows live equity, so every return_pct that divides
# by it moves; realized P&L itself is identical. Measured on STG wtvk2: capital_base 1097455.65 -> 1097266.72
# (x1.000172) reproduces each changed value to the 4th decimal (7.0589 -> 7.0601, 4.2548 -> 4.2555, ...).
perf.realized_by_account[*].return_pct
perf.realized_by_account_and_sec_type[*].return_pct
# IB's TotalCashValue passes straight through raw_broker.account (core model/core.py reads it as is); on PROD
# 99wkl the row was refreshed by the IB account snapshot at 17:53:21Z, 3 s before the after snapshot (+28.02).
model.*.account_summary.total_cash
# The rest of the same drift, measured on STG kk259 (18:27:21 -> 18:30:55Z, market hours; api/core/worker/ui
# commits identical to wtvk2). Two accounts' net liquidation rose 72.85 + 0.21 = 73.06, and current_equity,
# start_equity (+73.06) and capital_base (+73.05) followed. All 45 changed return_pct equal
# old x 1099010.24 / 1099083.29 to the 4th decimal; executions and every P&L amount were identical.
perf.calendar[*].return_pct
perf.calendar_by_sec_type[*].return_pct
perf.realized_by_sec_type[*].return_pct
perf.realized_by_strategy_opportunity[*].return_pct
perf.realized_by_trade[*].return_pct
perf.summary.return_pct
perf.unrealized.return_pct   # divides by current_equity, not capital_base (PROD 99wkl: 475367.75 / 1082689.77)
perf.transaction.capital_base
perf.transaction.start_equity
perf.unrealized.current_equity
# IB pass-throughs, like total_cash above.
model.*.account_summary.buying_power
model.*.account_summary.net_liquidation
